 de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar cuántos contratos se adjudicaron en diciembre y si algunos se repiten con el mismo adjudicatario. También se puede revisar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden necesidades similares o si hay patrones en la distribución de los adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 108 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 28.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.9 to 4.9. December accounts for 12% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 17. Contract [1], for 14,855.94 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of contracts with one awardee do not prove improper actions. These could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and awardees to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the specific goods or services described in contract [1] to ensure they align with the body's needs.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["OlTBo5DsLBqqb7rCcv76BA%3D%3D","FoNha%2BxIYLgzjChw4z%2FXvw%3D%3D","yIBBCMynZirVGIpKDxgsAQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}